{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the king of Egypt said to the midwives.</b> They were officers over all the midwives, for there is no doubt that there were more than five hundred midwives; rather, these two were officers over them to collect a tax for the king from their wages. And thus I have seen today in many places. And the mother and the daughter were by tradition, for it is correct:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:46.570160069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}